module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.FinitePresentationDescent
import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.EtaleAtlasCriterionUnconditional
import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.SiteConventionAlgebraicLimit

/-!
# Finite-presentation algebraic spaces over a limit, with no bound on the index

The module `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.FinitePresentationDescent` proves
Stacks 07SK for a cofiltered inverse system of quasi-compact, quasi-separated algebraic spaces
over `S` with affine transition morphisms, whose index category is bounded in cardinality by the
cofinality of the site's cutoff. This module states the three parts of 07SK with no bound on the
index, under the chapter's convention 07SD.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_model_of_finitePresentation_of_chartLimitsInSite`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_morphism_after_baseChange_of_chartLimitsInSite` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eventually_eq_of_baseChange_eq_of_chartLimitsInSite`: essential
  surjectivity, fullness and faithfulness with no bound on the index category, under the
  chapter's convention 07SD that the limits of the base changes of the stages to the affine
  objects of the site lie in the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAlgebraicSpace_limit_of_chartLimitsInSite`: Stacks 07SF under the
  same convention, at one quasi-compact stage: the limit of the system is an algebraic space.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_chartLimitsInSite`: the convention as
  written out here is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits`.

## Implementation notes

The convention is written out in full in each statement, as the hypothesis `hconv`, rather than
through `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits`, so that the statements show
exactly what they assume. The two agree by unfolding.

The three parts of 07SK are the forms `_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.FinitePresentationDescent`, without their
hypothesis that the limit is an algebraic space: that hypothesis is supplied by Stacks 07SF
under the convention,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAlgebraicSpace_limit_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits`.
The source has no such hypothesis, so these are the faithful statements.

This lives in its own module, not beside the bounded forms, so that the import closure of the
bounded module is not enlarged.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SK)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

/-! ### Stacks 07SK under the chapter's convention 07SD

The three bounded statements of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.FinitePresentationDescent` bound the cardinality of
the index category by the cofinality of the site's cutoff. Stacks 07SK has no such bound. It works
under the convention of Section 70.2 (tag 07SD) that every ring the chapter considers has its
spectrum in the big fppf site. For an inverse system with affine transition morphisms, the rings
formed in the proof of 07SK are the directed colimits of the rings of the base changes, over one
stage `i`, of the stages over `i` to an affine object `Z` of the site. The convention says that
their spectra, which are the limits of those base changes, lie in the site. The hypothesis `hconv`
below is that statement. It is written out in full and is not an assumption beyond the source: it
is the source's standing convention, read for this system. It says exactly what
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits` says, unfolded
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_chartLimitsInSite`).

The index bound of the three bounded statements implies `hconv`. The two are not equivalent:
take a ring `A` with `Spec A` in the site and the system of the spectra of its finitely
generated subrings. This system satisfies `hconv`, because every limit in question is a base
change of `Spec A` to an affine object of the site. Its index has cardinality `#A` when `A` is
infinite, and the cutoff may be singular, so `#A` may lie between the cofinality and the
cutoff.

`hconv` cannot be dropped either. For a field `F` of cardinality at least the cutoff, the
system of the spectra of the subrings generated by the finite subsets of `F` has, as its limit
in presheaves on the site, the presheaf represented by the empty scheme: a ring smaller than
the cutoff receives no ring homomorphism from `F` unless it is zero. Two distinct endomorphisms
of the affine line over a stage then agree after base change to the limit and at no stage. -/

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

section ChartLimitsInSite

attribute [local simp] pullback.lift_fst pullback.lift_snd
  pullback.lift_fst_assoc pullback.lift_snd_assoc

variable (B : AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : B.Contains S) (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
variable {I : Type u} [Category.{u} I] [IsCofiltered I]
variable (D : I ⥤ (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)

omit [IsCofiltered I] in
/-- **The convention 07SD, written out, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits`.** The hypothesis `hconv` of the
statements below states, for every limit cone of the diagram of base changes, that its apex lies
in the site. That is what `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.LimitInSite` says, both being the
size bound `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.size` below the cutoff, so the two agree by unfolding. -/
theorem siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_chartLimitsInSite
    (hconv : ∀ (i : I) (Z : AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS)
      (g : yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z) ⟶ D.obj i)
      (W : Over i ⥤ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS),
      (W ⋙ (AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙ yoneda) ≅
        (Over.post (X := i) D ⋙ Over.pullback g) ⋙
          Over.forget (yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z))) →
      ∀ c : Cone (((W ⋙ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS) ⋙
          AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.forget B S hS) ⋙ B.inclusion),
        IsLimit c → B.Contains c.pt) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits B S hS D :=
  hconv

/-- **Stacks 07SF, existence, under the convention 07SD.** The limit of the system is an
algebraic space as soon as one stage is quasi-compact: the base change to the limit of an affine
étale atlas of that stage is a surjective étale atlas of the limit by an object of the site,
because the projections from the limit are affine under the convention. -/
theorem isAlgebraicSpace_limit_of_chartLimitsInSite
    (hconv : ∀ (i : I) (Z : AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS)
      (g : yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z) ⟶ D.obj i)
      (W : Over i ⥤ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS),
      (W ⋙ (AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙ yoneda) ≅
        (Over.post (X := i) D ⋙ Over.pullback g) ⋙
          Over.forget (yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z))) →
      ∀ c : Cone (((W ⋙ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS) ⋙
          AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.forget B S hS) ⋙ B.inclusion),
        IsLimit c → B.Contains c.pt)
    (hD : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (D.obj i))
    (hAffine : ∀ {i j : I} (f : i ⟶ j), AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsAffineHom B S hS (D.map f))
    (i : I) (hQci : AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS (D.obj i)) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (limit D) := by
  obtain ⟨U₀, p₀, hU₀, hs₀, he₀⟩ :=
    (isQuasiCompactSpace_iff_exists_affine_etale_surjective_cover B S hS (D.obj i) (hD i)).mp hQci
  obtain ⟨U, p, q, hp⟩ :=
    isAffineHom_limitπ_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits B S hS D
      (siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_chartLimitsInSite B S hS D hconv) hAffine i ⟨U₀, hU₀⟩ p₀
  let P := MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
    (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)
  let Q := MorphismProperty.inverseImage (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
    (AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)
  let : P.presheaf.IsStableUnderBaseChange := P.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange (F := yoneda)
  let : Q.presheaf.IsStableUnderBaseChange := Q.relative_isStableUnderBaseChange (F := yoneda)
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.isAlgebraicSpace_of_surjective_etale_atlas B S hS
    (isSheaf_limit B S hS D fun i => (hD i).isSheaf) U.obj p
    (P.presheaf.of_isPullback hp.flip hs₀)
    (Q.presheaf.of_isPullback hp.flip ((isEtale_iff_presheaf_of_yoneda B S hS p₀).mp he₀))

/-- **The cardinality bounds of the bounded forms of Stacks 07SK imply the convention 07SD for
the system.** If the index category and its morphism types are smaller than the cofinality of
the cutoff, then every slice `Over i` is too, so the limit of any diagram of affine objects of the
site indexed by it lies in the site, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.size_lt_of_isLimit_of_isAffine`.
So the forms with suffix `_of_chartLimitsInSite` imply the bounded forms. -/
theorem chartLimitsInSite_of_lt_cof (hSize : Cardinal.mk I < B.cutoff.ord.cof)
    (hHomSize : ∀ i j : I, Cardinal.mk (i ⟶ j) < B.cutoff.ord.cof) :
    ∀ (i : I) (Z : AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS)
      (g : yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z) ⟶ D.obj i)
      (W : Over i ⥤ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS),
      (W ⋙ (AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙ yoneda) ≅
        (Over.post (X := i) D ⋙ Over.pullback g) ⋙
          Over.forget (yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z))) →
      ∀ c : Cone (((W ⋙ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS) ⋙
          AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.forget B S hS) ⋙ B.inclusion),
        IsLimit c → B.Contains c.pt := by
  intro i _ _ W _ c hc
  let V : Over i ⥤ Scheme.{u} := ((W ⋙ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS) ⋙
    AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.forget B S hS) ⋙ B.inclusion
  have hV : ∀ j, IsAffine (V.obj j) := fun j => (W.obj j).property
  have hsize : ∀ j, (V.obj j).size < B.cutoff := fun j => (W.obj j).obj.left.property
  exact Scheme.size_lt_of_isLimit_of_isAffine B.aleph0_lt_cutoff V hV
    (mk_over_lt B.aleph0_lt_cutoff_cof hSize hHomSize i) hsize hc

/-- **Stacks 07SK, fullness, with no bound on the index.** A morphism between the base changes
to the limit of two algebraic spaces of finite presentation over a stage comes from a morphism
at a later stage.

This strengthens `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_morphism_after_baseChange`: the cardinality
bounds on the index category are replaced by `hconv`. `hconv` is the convention 07SD of the
chapter: the limits of the base changes of the stages to the affine objects of the site lie in
the site. It is not an assumption beyond the source. It is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits` unfolded, and the index bounds imply it.

It is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_morphism_after_baseChange_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits`
without the hypothesis that the limit is an algebraic space, which Stacks 07SF under the
convention supplies. -/
@[stacks 07SK "fullness, with no bound on the index: the 07SD convention in place of the \
  cardinality bounds of exists_morphism_after_baseChange"]
public theorem exists_morphism_after_baseChange_of_chartLimitsInSite
    (hconv : ∀ (i : I) (Z : AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS)
      (g : yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z) ⟶ D.obj i)
      (W : Over i ⥤ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS),
      (W ⋙ (AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙ yoneda) ≅
        (Over.post (X := i) D ⋙ Over.pullback g) ⋙
          Over.forget (yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z))) →
      ∀ c : Cone (((W ⋙ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS) ⋙
          AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.forget B S hS) ⋙ B.inclusion),
        IsLimit c → B.Contains c.pt)
    (hD : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (D.obj i))
    (hAffine : ∀ {i j : I} (f : i ⟶ j), AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsAffineHom B S hS (D.map f))
    (hQc : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS (D.obj i))
    (hQs : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ (D.obj i))
    (i : I) (Yᵢ Zᵢ : Over (D.obj i))
    (hY : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Yᵢ.left)
    (hZ' : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Zᵢ.left)
    (hYfp : AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFinitePresentation B S hS Yᵢ.hom)
    (hZfp : AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFinitePresentation B S hS Zᵢ.hom)
    (f : (Over.pullback (limit.π D i)).obj Yᵢ ⟶
      (Over.pullback (limit.π D i)).obj Zᵢ) :
    ∃ (j : I) (e : j ⟶ i)
      (g : (Over.pullback (D.map e)).obj Yᵢ ⟶
        (Over.pullback (D.map e)).obj Zᵢ)
      (α : (Over.pullback (limit.π D j)).obj
          ((Over.pullback (D.map e)).obj Yᵢ) ≅
        (Over.pullback (limit.π D i)).obj Yᵢ)
      (β : (Over.pullback (limit.π D j)).obj
          ((Over.pullback (D.map e)).obj Zᵢ) ≅
        (Over.pullback (limit.π D i)).obj Zᵢ),
      (α.hom.left ≫ pullback.fst Yᵢ.hom (limit.π D i) =
        pullback.fst ((Over.pullback (D.map e)).obj Yᵢ).hom (limit.π D j) ≫
          pullback.fst Yᵢ.hom (D.map e)) ∧
      (β.hom.left ≫ pullback.fst Zᵢ.hom (limit.π D i) =
        pullback.fst ((Over.pullback (D.map e)).obj Zᵢ).hom (limit.π D j) ≫
          pullback.fst Zᵢ.hom (D.map e)) ∧
      α.hom ≫ f = (Over.pullback (limit.π D j)).map g ≫ β.hom :=
  have hconv := siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_chartLimitsInSite B S hS D hconv
  exists_morphism_after_baseChange_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits
    (B := B) (S := S) (hS := hS) (hZ := hZ) (D := D)
    (hD := hD) (hAffine := hAffine) (hQc := hQc) (hQs := hQs) (hconv := hconv)
    (hDlim := isAlgebraicSpace_limit_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits B S hS D hconv hD hAffine hQc)
    i Yᵢ Zᵢ hY hZ' hYfp hZfp f

/-- **Stacks 07SK, faithfulness, with no bound on the index.** Two morphisms between
algebraic spaces of finite presentation over a stage whose base changes to the limit agree
already agree at a later stage.

This strengthens `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eventually_eq_of_baseChange_eq`: the cardinality
bounds on the index category are replaced by `hconv`. `hconv` is the convention 07SD of the
chapter: the limits of the base changes of the stages to the affine objects of the site lie in
the site. It is not an assumption beyond the source. It is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits` unfolded, and the index bounds imply it.
Without it the statement is false; see the notes opening this section.

It is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eventually_eq_of_baseChange_eq_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits`
with the convention written out. -/
@[stacks 07SK "faithfulness, with no bound on the index: the 07SD convention in place of the \
  cardinality bounds of eventually_eq_of_baseChange_eq"]
public theorem eventually_eq_of_baseChange_eq_of_chartLimitsInSite
    (hconv : ∀ (i : I) (Z : AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS)
      (g : yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z) ⟶ D.obj i)
      (W : Over i ⥤ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS),
      (W ⋙ (AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙ yoneda) ≅
        (Over.post (X := i) D ⋙ Over.pullback g) ⋙
          Over.forget (yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z))) →
      ∀ c : Cone (((W ⋙ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS) ⋙
          AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.forget B S hS) ⋙ B.inclusion),
        IsLimit c → B.Contains c.pt)
    (hD : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (D.obj i))
    (hAffine : ∀ {i j : I} (f : i ⟶ j), AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsAffineHom B S hS (D.map f))
    (hQc : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS (D.obj i))
    (hQs : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ (D.obj i))
    (i : I) (Yᵢ Zᵢ : Over (D.obj i))
    (hY : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Yᵢ.left)
    (hZ' : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Zᵢ.left)
    (hYfp : AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFinitePresentation B S hS Yᵢ.hom)
    (hZfp : AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFinitePresentation B S hS Zᵢ.hom)
    (f g : Yᵢ ⟶ Zᵢ)
    (hfg : (Over.pullback (limit.π D i)).map f =
      (Over.pullback (limit.π D i)).map g) :
    ∃ (j : I) (e : j ⟶ i),
      (Over.pullback (D.map e)).map f =
        (Over.pullback (D.map e)).map g :=
  eventually_eq_of_baseChange_eq_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits
    (B := B) (S := S) (hS := hS) (hZ := hZ) (D := D)
    (hD := hD) (hAffine := hAffine) (hQc := hQc) (hQs := hQs)
    (hconv := siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_chartLimitsInSite B S hS D hconv)
    i Yᵢ Zᵢ hY hZ' hYfp hZfp f g hfg

/-- **Stacks 07SK, essential surjectivity, with no bound on the index.** Every algebraic space
of finite presentation over the limit is the base change of an algebraic space of finite
presentation over some stage.

This strengthens `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_model_of_finitePresentation`: the cardinality
bounds on the index category are replaced by `hconv`. `hconv` is the convention 07SD of the
chapter: the limits of the base changes of the stages to the affine objects of the site lie in
the site. It is not an assumption beyond the source. It is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits` unfolded, and the index bounds imply it.

It is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_model_of_finitePresentation_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits`
without the hypothesis that the limit is an algebraic space, which Stacks 07SF under the
convention supplies. -/
@[stacks 07SK "essential surjectivity, with no bound on the index: the 07SD convention in \
  place of the cardinality bounds of exists_model_of_finitePresentation"]
public theorem exists_model_of_finitePresentation_of_chartLimitsInSite
    (hconv : ∀ (i : I) (Z : AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS)
      (g : yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z) ⟶ D.obj i)
      (W : Over i ⥤ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf B S hS),
      (W ⋙ (AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙ yoneda) ≅
        (Over.post (X := i) D ⋙ Over.pullback g) ⋙
          Over.forget (yoneda.obj ((AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj Z))) →
      ∀ c : Cone (((W ⋙ AlgebraicGeometry.BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS) ⋙
          AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.forget B S hS) ⋙ B.inclusion),
        IsLimit c → B.Contains c.pt)
    (hD : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (D.obj i))
    (hAffine : ∀ {i j : I} (f : i ⟶ j), AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsAffineHom B S hS (D.map f))
    (hQc : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS (D.obj i))
    (hQs : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ (D.obj i))
    (Y : Over (limit D))
    (hY : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Y.left)
    (hFp : AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFinitePresentation B S hS Y.hom) :
    ∃ (i : I) (Yᵢ : Over (D.obj i)),
      AlgebraicGeometry.IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Yᵢ.left ∧
        AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFinitePresentation B S hS Yᵢ.hom ∧
        Nonempty (Y ≅ (Over.pullback (limit.π D i)).obj Yᵢ) :=
  have hconv := siteContainsBaseChangeLimits_of_chartLimitsInSite B S hS D hconv
  exists_model_of_finitePresentation_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits
    (B := B) (S := S) (hS := hS) (hZ := hZ) (D := D)
    (hD := hD) (hAffine := hAffine) (hQc := hQc) (hQs := hQs) (hconv := hconv)
    (hDlim := isAlgebraicSpace_limit_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits B S hS D hconv hD hAffine hQc)
    Y hY hFp

end ChartLimitsInSite

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
